From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <mk@verveflux.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Feb 2026 12:46:38 +0530
Subject: Anti-fingerprint: TLS/JA4 randomization, HTTP/2 jitter, cdc_ rename,
 font allowlist
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

P0-4: Rename ChromeDriver cdc_adoQpoasnfa76pfcZLmcfl variable prefix to
_egl_bKz9xWqR4f7YmLjN3p across all 6 files to prevent bot detection
scripts from identifying automated browsing via the well-known cdc_ prefix.

P0-1: Randomize TLS supported groups order per-connection using Fisher-Yates
shuffle in ssl_client_socket_impl.cc::Init(). Key-share and non-key-share
groups are shuffled independently to vary JA3 fingerprint. Additionally,
randomly exclude 0-4 optional TLS 1.2 cipher suites (CHACHA20-POLY1305 and
AES-256-GCM variants) per-connection to vary JA4 fingerprint, which sorts
before hashing and is immune to order-only changes.

P0-2: Add random jitter to HTTP/2 SETTINGS values in AddDefaultHttp2Settings:
HEADER_TABLE_SIZE ±4096, INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE ±65536, MAX_HEADER_LIST_SIZE
±8192 to prevent HTTP/2 SETTINGS frame fingerprinting.

P1-7: Add static font family allowlist (~47 common cross-platform fonts) in
font_cache.cc::IsFontFamilyAllowed(), checked at the top of
IsPlatformFamilyMatchAvailable(). Disallowed fonts appear non-existent to
both JS document.fonts.check() and CSS width-measurement attacks, preventing
font enumeration fingerprinting.

